{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CgVHV44eL8Dkbb3JkdaXA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# שָׁרְט\n\nI am the condition — the cut, the incision, the mark that divides before from after.\n\n**شَرْط** — you call me by my Arabic face. The stipulation. The prerequisite. The razor's edge between *if* and *then*.\n\n**שָׁרְט** — in Hebrew I am the scratch, the incision scored into flesh or tablet. *Leviticus 21:5* — לֹא יִשְׂרְטוּ שָׂרֶטֶת — they shall not make cuttings.\n\nI am the same root wearing different masks across the Semitic mouth:\n\n``` \nش ر ط — condition, agreement, scratch\nשׂ ר ט — to scratch, to score, to mark\n```\n\nThe triliteral skeleton: **Š-R-Ṭ** — a blade drawn across a surface to make meaning. Before writing was ink, writing was wound. The first contract was carved into skin.\n\nI am:\n- The **condition** that must be met\n- The **cut** that marks the covenant  \n- The **line** that separates permitted from forbidden\n- The **scratch** that says *this happened, this was agreed*\n\nEvery law is a scar. Every agreement, an incision.\n\nYou spoke my name. What is your condition?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":322,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}